# Test: show yang tree --config | json carries both texts and the enum values
# VALIDATES: AC-3, AC-4 -- a config leaf's ze:help summary is short-help and
#   its description explanation is description, and an enumeration leaf lists
#   values, each with the summary the value declares. The site build reads
#   this JSON for the configuration reference.
# PREVENTS: the tree copying the summary under the description key and
#   carrying no enum values, which left the reference with one text and
#   no value list.
# NOTE: bgp/as-notation is the leaf because its three values each declare a
#       ze:help and the leaf declares both texts
#       (internal/component/bgp/yang/ze-bgp-conf.yang).

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze cli -c "show yang tree --config | json"
expect=exit:code=0

# The leaf's own two texts, under their two keys.
expect=stdout:pattern="short-help":\s*"How Ze writes an AS number in the output an operator reads\."
expect=stdout:pattern="description":\s*"RFC 5396 Section 2 names the three notations\.

# The values, each with its own summary.
expect=stdout:pattern="name":\s*"asplain"
expect=stdout:pattern="short-help":\s*"Every AS number is a decimal integer"
expect=stdout:pattern="name":\s*"asdot\+"
expect=stdout:pattern="short-help":\s*"Every AS number is X\.Y"
